{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34992-the-relationships-guide-of-world-of-darkness","id":34992,"title":"The Relationships Guide of World Of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T10:14:36-08:00","id":34992,"title":"The Relationships Guide of World Of Darkness","content":"Me and a friend been discussing a lot the subjects of the lore in world of darkness, its myths and legends.<br /> On my end theres a couple of things i want to understand...You see, most game books explain how a group or race views others. we been wondering<br /> A ) How do changelings view demons, their existance and what are they (from their point of view)<br /> B ) How demons View changelings, how do they came to be and what are they exactly (from their point of view)<br /> C ) How Wraiths view Demons/Changelings/Mummies, how do they came to be and what are they from their point of view, and vicesersa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T11:44:29-08:00","id":35031,"title":"","content":"As far as I have figured, the fatsplats (<i>V:tM, W:tA, M:tA, W:tO, C:tD, H:tR, D:tF, etc.</i>) are often parallel, but different versions of the other lines in the WoD that <u>sometimes</u> cross, but don't always match up. In V:tM, the lupines* aren't necessarily Garou, and in W:tA, the vampires* aren't necessarily Cainites, etc.. What a Demon thinks of the fairies* might be quite different than what he might think of the Changelings IF the two fatsplats actually crossed, as well as what the Changelings may think of the demons* if they encountered them, etc.. Each game line might interpret the representation of the other fatsplats different than how they would be seen natively in their own systems.<br /> <br /> *<i>note the lower-cased usage to denote a generalized name rather than the specific self-title of that group.</i><br /> <br /> So, to try to help you in your answer to your questions, it will partly depend on how that &quot;other&quot; concept is interpreted within the native Fatsplat (how fairies, the representation of Changeling: the Dreaming concepts, are portrayed within the Demon: the Fallen fatsplat, etc..)<br /> <br /> So, Changelings may view demons (or their representation of Demons within C:tD) as some sort of lost fae, or Dreaming creations, even though that wouldn't match up with what is Factual within D:tF.<br /> <br /> As for the specifics of what each line thinks of the others... well, I'm sure your issue comes from the fact that some books (like Changeling) didn't really get to address the new lines, but maybe there's something packed into a supplement somewhere that those afficianatos might know about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T12:11:25-08:00","id":35052,"title":"","content":"Yeah the thing is WtO and CtD never got a Revised Edition. WtO ended in 1999 with <i>Ends of Empire</i> which itself was the catalyst for the Revised Edition era and the later gamelines that sprung up, including DtF. The closest thing we have to a WtO book in the Rev Ed is the Orpheus gameline, the spiritual successor to WtO that kind of is but isn't a sequel to WtO. Of course if you are a WtO fan I highly recommend <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?cPath=1_4\" target=\"_blank\">Orpheus</a>.<br /> <br /> While the only CtD book we have in the Rev Ed era is the <i>Time of Judgement</i> which ends CtD along with HtR, DtF, KotE and MtR. Hence we have very little on their relationships (at least from their perspectives) with the newer lines. Maybe that will change with Wr20 and C20 as I've seen references to the Imbued in several X20 books despite the default setting being before they existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T12:25:23-08:00","id":35069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/34992-the-relationships-guide-of-world-of-darkness?p=35052#post35052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the only CtD book we have in the Rev Ed era is the <i>Time of Judgement</i> which ends CtD along with HtR, DtF, KotE and MtR. Hence we have very little on their relationships (at least from their perspectives) with the newer lines. Maybe that will change with Wr20 and C20 as I've seen references to the Imbued in several X20 books despite the default setting being before they existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the core books refer to things so that those rules are there for STs to use if they want to... including both types of Malks, dead Bloodlines and Tribes and whatnot. So, even if W20's default timeline steps back before ToJ, it may begin to incorporate things that lead-up to it, or even a ret-conned setting that includes elements that weren't there before. Again, each of those X20 settings are written from each line's perspective, so they may not even be canonically correct to the others (again, see above post.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:25:13-08:00","id":35094,"title":"","content":"I recall Changeling 2nd Ed stating somewhere that Changelings are quite aware of other supernatural creatures, which is a bit atypical in WoD. They call these others &quot;prodigals&quot; and assume that they are fae or changelings who have forgotten their true nature. Usually, they are pitied and avoided, but changelings can be inquisitive and capricious at times so sticking one's nose in the business of other supernatural creatures isn't unheard of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T17:49:09-08:00","id":35223,"title":"","content":"In earlier versions of all the core books and system (say back when there were just 5), all supernaturals were at least aware of each other. Some books gave examples for how to run NPCs of the others within that system, but actually recommended checking out the other system books if more detail was needed than their in-system template. As Revised came about, such encouragement for system to system reference seemed to be omitted. Since Hunter, Mummy and Demon came in around this time, they too omitted direct reference of association with the other systems, especially those that were being discontinued. Instead the references became as Torakhan stated. That Lupines were not necessarily Garou and Vampires not necessarily Cainites etc. I suppose if you really want to figure out what Demons are to Changelings, the closest might be in the tiny supplement book of Denizens of the Dreaming. (Which I originally thought would be more about the Dreaming and different Bygones and Chimera, but instead was more of a Misc. Fae collection.) While it might not have anything that equates to Demons, how the general fae view the other Denizens as alien outsiders might be how they would view Demons as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}